                },
                "comment_count": 0,
                "committer": {
                    "date": "2026-08-26T11:58:32Z",
                    "email": "github.elitism514@passmail.com",
                    "name": "NoxToxCipher"
                },
                "message": "fix(LAN_discovery): use interface IP and bitwise masking for Windows broadcast calculation\n\nIn fetch_broadcast_info on Windows, the subnet broadcast address was computed using addition against the gateway IP: gateway_ip + ~subnet_ip - 1.\n\nThis caused two issues: 1) If the gateway IP was higher than .1 (e.g. .254), the addition overflowed into the preceding octet, producing an invalid broadcast address. 2) If the interface had no default gateway configured (e.g. offline LAN or direct cable connection), GatewayList was 0.0.0.0, which broke LAN discovery entirely.\n\nUse the adapter's own IPv4 address and standard bitwise subnet masking ((ip & mask) | ~mask) to compute the subnet broadcast address.",
                "tree": {
                    "sha": "fda1c3751fd93e17213f9ef75aae5df9850f46d7",
                    "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/TokTok/c-toxcore/git/trees/fda1c3751fd93e17213f9ef75aae5df9850f46d7"
                },
                "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/TokTok/c-toxcore/git/commits/f9f65092c26274108bc96cea47e3a1200e7309fa",
                "verification": {
                    "payload": "tree fda1c3751fd93e17213f9ef75aae5df9850f46d7\nparent 02daf25560e2b9978fa0666948614b286b71ca9b\nauthor NoxToxCipher <github.elitism514@passmail.com> 1787585106 +1000\ncommitter NoxToxCipher <github.elitism514@passmail.com> 1787745512 +1000\n\nfix(LAN_discovery): use interface IP and bitwise masking for Windows broadcast calculation\n\nIn fetch_broadcast_info on Windows, the subnet broadcast address was computed using addition against the gateway IP: gateway_ip + ~subnet_ip - 1.\n\nThis caused two issues: 1) If the gateway IP was higher than .1 (e.g. .254), the addition overflowed into the preceding octet, producing an invalid broadcast address. 2) If the interface had no default gateway configured (e.g. offline LAN or direct cable connection), GatewayList was 0.0.0.0, which broke LAN discovery entirely.\n\nUse the adapter's own IPv4 address and standard bitwise subnet masking ((ip & mask) | ~mask) to compute the subnet broadcast address.\n",
                    "reason": "valid",
                    "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQQu7bWBkJw+oLcWkG0tXapn7VlH/gUCao7U6AAKCRAtXapn7VlH\n/gx2AP9fTc/FU17a9lXrzu12tkpt7RTzMOojvGMis3IFvcn/uwEAi3e3/Ayjy/Ak\ngPQhxR+soN7mk3d+HLzBKwCkC8HtHQ0=\n=U0mD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----",
